# The ODbL evidence chain records SHA-256 values for acquisition responses,
# request logs and the shipped pilot datasets, and the tests compare raw bytes.
# Checkouts must therefore stay byte-exact regardless of core.autocrlf: a fresh
# Windows checkout once rewrote LF to CRLF and invalidated the pinned hashes.
data/** -text

# C7.3.1 exercises the Flutter model against the VERBATIM backend response body
# stored as a fixture and documents its SHA-256, so that fixture must
# materialize byte-exactly on every platform too (same class as above).
test/fixtures/*.json -text
